{"abstract":"Active learning aims to select the minimum amount of data to train a model that performs similarly to a model trained with the entire dataset. We study the potential of active learning for image segmentation in underwater infrastructure inspection tasks, where large amounts of data are typically collected. The pipeline inspection images are usually semantically repetitive but with great variations in quality. We use mutual information as the acquisition function, calculated using Monte Carlo dropout. HyperSeg is trained using active learning with an underwater pipeline inspection dataset of over 50,000 images. To allow reproducibility and assess the framework’s effectiveness, the CamVid dataset was also utilized. For the pipeline dataset, HyperSeg with active learning achieved 67.5% meanIoU using 12.5% of the data, and 61.4 % with the same amount of randomly selected images. This shows that using active learning for segmentation models in underwater inspection tasks can lower the cost significantly.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ribeiro Marnet, Luiza","Grasshof, Stella","Brodskiy, Yuri","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730182"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active learning","Computer vision","Underwater inspection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["EIVA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uncertainty driven active learning for image segmentation in underwater inspection","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.14002.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730182","ids":["itu-950ebbcc-5a10-4ece-919f-f1beb600add2"],"keyword":["Active learning","Computer vision","Underwater inspection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-15FA40FC63DF05822113463C38168637"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.14002.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.14002","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["EIVA"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luiza","key":"ribeiromarnetpau","last":"Ribeiro Marnet","name":"Ribeiro Marnet, Luiza","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","name_org":"Graßhof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuri","key":"brodskiypau","last":"Brodskiy","name":"Brodskiy, Yuri","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-950ebbcc-5a10-4ece-919f-f1beb600add2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Uncertainty Driven Active Learning for Image Segmentation in Underwater Inspection","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730182","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Denoising Diffusion Models (DDMs) have emerged as a strong competitor to Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs). However, despite their widespread use in image synthesis and editing applications, their latent space is still not as well understood. Recently, a semantic latent space for DDMs, coined ‘h-space’, was shown to facilitate semantic image editing in a way reminiscent of GANs. The h-space is comprised of the bottleneck activations in the DDM’s denoiser across all timesteps of the diffusion process. In this paper, we explore the properties of h-space and propose several novel methods for finding meaningful semantic directions within it. We start by studying unsupervised methods for revealing interpretable semantic directions in pretrained DDMs. Specifically, we show that interpretable directions emerge as the principal components in the latent space. Additionally, we provide a novel method for discovering image-specific semantic directions by spectral analysis of the Jacobian of the denoiser w.r.t. the latent code. Next, we extend the analysis by finding directions in a supervised fashion in unconditional DDMs. We demonstrate how such directions can be found by annotating generated samples with a domain-specific attribute classifier. We further show how to semantically disentangle the found directions by simple linear projection. Our approaches are applicable without requiring any architectural modifications, text-based guidance, CLIP-based optimization, or model fine-tuning.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Haas, René","Huberman-Spiegelglas, Inbar","Mulayoff, Rotem","Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian","Michaeli, Tomer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747266"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technion - Israel Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Diffusion","Faces","Latent Space","disentanglement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discovering interpretable directions in the semantic latent space of diffusion models","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://brosdocs.net/fg2024/267.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747266","identifier":[{"id":"85199476974","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-db60d9da-0207-4961-832b-587c2449946f"],"keyword":["diffusion","disentanglement","faces","latent space"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-33499E9963BD2CCB6EED9145511615F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://brosdocs.net/fg2024/267.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"il","key":"technion israel institute of technology","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Technion - Israel Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"haaspau","last":"Haas","name":"Haas, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Inbar","key":"hubermanspiegelglaspau","last":"Huberman-Spiegelglas","name":"Huberman-Spiegelglas, Inbar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rotem","key":"mulayoffpau","last":"Mulayoff","name":"Mulayoff, Rotem","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","name_org":"Graßhof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomer","key":"michaelipau","last":"Michaeli","name":"Michaeli, Tomer","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"18th IEEE International Conference on Automatic Face and Gesture Recognition"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-db60d9da-0207-4961-832b-587c2449946f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Discovering Interpretable Directions in the Semantic Latent Space of Diffusion Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747266","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In a highly digitalised world, this paper aims at closing the gap towards automatic digitisation from 2D architectural drawings. We present the new image dataset Plan, and Elevation Representations of Doors And Windows (Perdaw) which provides a baseline for different classification problems with varying complexity. We investigate the performance of three machine learning models in distinguishing different types of doors and windows in their plan and elevation views. Our findings show that Inception V3 slightly outperforms MobileNet V2, which suggests that the latter solves the same classification tasks with less computational resources with only a minimal compromise in accuracy. Among the three investigated models, ResNet50 yields the lowest quality metrics within a small margin. Overall, all models perform better at classifying building components in their elevation views compared to their plan views. We consistently observed that the models yield the best results with 100{\\%} accuracy for the binary classification problems, and dropped to close to 70{\\%} accuracy for the 40-class classification problems.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Filip, Alexandru","Grasshof, Stella"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764512"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Architecture","Convolutional neural networks","Deep learning","Floor plans","Machine learning","Object Classification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards digitisation of technical drawings in architecture evaluation of cnn classification on the perdaw dataset","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85198940286","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764512","identifier":[{"id":"85198940286","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cf5f4e0e-af5a-4efd-b8b6-6d48533bd37a"],"keyword":["Architectural Symbols","Architecture","Convolutional Neural Networks","Deep Learning","Floor plans","Machine learning","Object Classification","Technical Symbols"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CCF50F22488A559E97D9329652A49317"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexandru","key":"filippau","last":"Filip","name":"Filip, Alexandru","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","name_org":"Graßhof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lazaros","key":"iliadispedh","last":"Iliadis","name":"Iliadis, Lazaros","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ilias","key":"maglogiannispedh","last":"Maglogiannis","name":"Maglogiannis, Ilias","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Antonios","key":"papaleonidaspedh","last":"Papaleonidas","name":"Papaleonidas, Antonios","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Elias","key":"pimenidispedh","last":"Pimenidis","name":"Pimenidis, Elias","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Chrisina","key":"jaynepedh","last":"Jayne","name":"Jayne, Chrisina","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-62495-7_22","eisbn":["9783031624957"],"isbn":["9783031624940"],"issn":["18650929"],"pages":"288-300","publisher":"Springer","series":"Communications in Computer and Information Science","status":"p","title":"Engineering Applications of Neural Networks"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198940286"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cf5f4e0e-af5a-4efd-b8b6-6d48533bd37a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Digitisation of Technical Drawings in Architecture: Evaluation of CNN Classification on the Perdaw Dataset","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764512","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Reconstructing 3D trajectories from video is often cumbersome and expensive, relying on complex or multi-camera setups. This paper proposes SynthNet, an end-to-end pipeline for monocular reconstruction of 3D tennis ball trajectories. The pipeline consists of two parts: Hit and bounce detection and 3D trajectory reconstruction. The hit and bounce detection is performed by a GRU-based model, which segments the videos into individual shots. Next, a fully connected neural network reconstructs the 3D trajectory through a novel physics-based training approach relying on purely synthetic training data. Instability in the training loop caused by relying on Euler-time integration and camera projections is circumvented by our synthetic approach, which directly calculates loss from estimated initial conditions, improving stability and performance.\\\\ In experiments, SynthNet is compared to an existing reconstruction baseline on a number of conventional and customized metrics defined to validate our synthetic approach. SynthNet outperforms the baseline based on our own proposed metrics and in a qualitative inspection of the reconstructed 3D trajectories.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ertner, Morten Holck","Konglevoll, Sofus","Ibh, Magnus","Grasshof, Stella"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776386"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Physics informed neural networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synthnet leveraging synthetic data for 000000000003d trajectory estimation from monocular video","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3689061.3689073","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776386","ids":["itu-356d9e1a-c065-44dc-9a7c-1664547f1bb5"],"keyword":["GRU-based shot segmentation","Monocular 3D trajectory reconstruction","Physics-informed neural networks","Synthetic data-driven learning","Tennis ball trajectory estimation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-66C83059992B41639EF2B8DC72CADB76"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3689061.3689073","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Holck","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","name":"Ertner, Morten Holck","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofus","key":"konglevollpau","last":"Konglevoll","name":"Konglevoll, Sofus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"ibhpau","last":"Ibh","locid":"91d18624-3489-48a8-834d-8737581b8ff2","name":"Ibh, Magnus","orcid":"0009-0002-0334-4151","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","name_org":"Graßhof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9798400711985"],"isbn":["9798400711985"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 7th ACM International Workshop on Multimedia Content Analysis in Sports"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85210844211"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-356d9e1a-c065-44dc-9a7c-1664547f1bb5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"SynthNet: Leveraging Synthetic Data for 3D Trajectory Estimation from Monocular Video","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776386","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents, RallyTemPose, a transformer encoder-decoder model for predicting future badminton strokes based on previous rally actions. The model uses court position, skeleton poses, and player-specific embeddings to learn stroke and player-specific latent representations in a spatiotemporal encoder module. The representations are then used to condition the subsequent strokes in a decoder module through rally-aware fusion blocks, which provide additional relevant strategic and technical considerations to make more informed predictions. RallyTemPose shows improved forecasting accuracy compared to traditional sequential methods on two real-world badminton datasets. The performance boost can also be attributed to the inclusion of improved stroke embeddings extracted from the latent representation of a pre-trained large-language model subjected to detailed text descriptions of stroke descriptions. In the discussion, the latent representations learned by the encoder module show useful properties regarding player analysis and comparisons. The code can be found at: This https url.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ibh, Magnus","Graßhof, Stella","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Madeleine, Pascal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-786364"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-18","place":"Seattle, WA, USA","start":"2024-06-17","title":"2024 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops (CVPRW)","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer vision","Conferences","Data models","Predictive models","Skeleton","Spatiotemporal phenomena","Transformers"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a stroke of genius predicting the next move in badminton","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-786364","identifier":[{"id":"85206465133","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d6976834-1abf-4b08-802c-345f77a4891c"],"keyword":["Computer vision","Conferences","Data models","Predictive models","Skeleton","Spatiotemporal phenomena","Transformers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-79706F66D6C1EFA9D47A0A01554C70CD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, ExerciseTech"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"ibhpau","last":"Ibh","name":"Ibh, Magnus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","name":"Graßhof, Stella","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pascal","key":"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","locid":"2fa369c5-96e8-43bb-8c9d-1331827e6802","name":"Madeleine, Pascal","orcid":"0000-0002-2164-234X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cvprw63382.2024.00342","eisbn":["9798350365474"],"isbn":["9798350365481"],"issn":["21607516"],"pages":"3376-3385","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops","status":"p","title":"2024 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops (CVPRW)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206465133"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d6976834-1abf-4b08-802c-345f77a4891c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A stroke of genius : Predicting the next move in badminton","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-786364","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a transformer encoder-decoder model for predicting future badminton strokes based on previous rally actions. The model uses court position skeleton poses and player-specific embeddings to learn stroke and player-specific latent representations in a spatiotemporal encoder module. The representations are then used to condition the subsequent strokes in a decoder module through rally-aware fusion blocks which provide additional relevant strategic and technical considerations to make more informed predictions. RallyTemPose shows improved forecasting accuracy compared to traditional sequential methods on two real-world badminton datasets. The performance boost can also be attributed to the inclusion of improved stroke embeddings extracted from the latent representation of a pre-trained large-language model subjected to detailed text descriptions of stroke descriptions. In the discussion the latent representations learned by the encoder module show useful properties regarding player analysis and comparisons.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ibh, Magnus","Grasshof, Stella","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764505"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Badminton","Transformer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a stroke of genius predicting the next move in badminton","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024W/CVsports/html/Ibh_A_Stroke_of_Genius_Predicting_the_Next_Move_in_Badminton_CVPRW_2024_paper.html","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764505","identifier":[{"id":"85206465133","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-467a45c0-0c66-4182-aa1f-8ac89dc0bac7"],"keyword":["badminton","transformer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-65CC6E1FEDAE3F23B6010B4306B1B067"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024W/CVsports/html/Ibh_A_Stroke_of_Genius_Predicting_the_Next_Move_in_Badminton_CVPRW_2024_paper.html","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024W/CVsports/papers/Ibh_A_Stroke_of_Genius_Predicting_the_Next_Move_in_Badminton_CVPRW_2024_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"ibhpau","last":"Ibh","locid":"91d18624-3489-48a8-834d-8737581b8ff2","name":"Ibh, Magnus","orcid":"0009-0002-0334-4151","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","name_org":"Graßhof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"3376-3385","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) Workshops"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-467a45c0-0c66-4182-aa1f-8ac89dc0bac7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A stroke of genius: Predicting the next move in badminton","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764505","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Labeling images for every new task or data pattern a model needs to learn is a significant time bottleneck in real-world applications. Moreover, acquiring the necessary data for training the models can be challenging. Ideally, one would train the models with simulated images and adapt them for the desired real tasks using the least possible amount of data. Active learning can be used to solve this problem with minimal effort. In this work, we train SegFormer for pipeline segmentation with synthetic images from an underwater simulated environment and fine-tune the model with real underwater pipeline images recorded in a marina. The evaluation shows that selecting real data with active learning for fine-tuning the model gives better results than randomly selecting the images. As part of the work, we release the dataset recorded in the marina, MarinaPipe, which will be publicly available.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ribeiro Marnet, Luiza","Grasshof, Stella","Brodskiy, Yuri","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764506"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active learning","Computer vision","Image segmentation","Underwater inspection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["EIVA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bridging the sim to real gap for underwater image segmentation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"funding_acknowledgement":["funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Skłodowska-Curie grant agreement No. 956200"],"id":"S01-000.00-764506","identifier":[{"id":"85206447240","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4be18a27-833b-4475-944f-6314d0445bcf"],"keyword":["Underwater inspection","active learning","computer vision","image segmentation","sim-to-real"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FB6E8E748F7A58E12007FA6000723D75"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["EIVA"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luiza","key":"ribeiromarnetpau","last":"Ribeiro Marnet","name":"Ribeiro Marnet, Luiza","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","name_org":"Graßhof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuri","key":"brodskiypau","last":"Brodskiy","name":"Brodskiy, Yuri","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-4be18a27-833b-4475-944f-6314d0445bcf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bridging the Sim-to-Real GAP for Underwater Image Segmentation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764506","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents TemPose, a novel skeleton-based transformer model designed for fine-grained motion recognition to improve understanding of the detailed player actions in badminton. The model utilizes multiple temporal and interaction layers to capture variable-length multi-person human actions while minimizing reliance on non-human visual context. TemPose is evaluated on two fine-grained badminton datasets, where it significantly outperforms other baseline models by incorporating additional input streams, such as the shuttlecock position, into the temporal transformer layers of the model. Additionally, TemPose demonstrates great versatility by achieving competitive results compared to other state-of-the-art skeleton-based models on the large-scale action recognition benchmark NTU RGB+D. Experiments are conducted to explore how different model parameter configurations affect TemPose's performance. Additionally, a qualitative analysis of the temporal attention maps suggests that the model learns to prioritize frames of specific poses relevant to different actions while formulating an intuition of each individual's importance in the sequences. Overall, TemPose is an intuitive and versatile architecture that has the potential to be further developed and incorporated into other methods for managing human motion in sports with state-of-the-art results.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ibh, Magnus","Grasshof, Stella","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Madeleine, Pascal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718893"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fine grained action recognition","Human motion in sports","Skeleton based motion recognition","Temporal attention maps","Transformer model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tempose a new skeleton based transformer model designed for fine grained motion recognition in badminton","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102753157/Ibh_TemPose_A_New_Skeleton-Based_Transformer_Model_Designed_for_Fine-Grained_Motion_CVPRW_2023_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718893","ids":["itu-904a4314-ec77-4601-b2d6-5809a2b83adc"],"keyword":["Fine-grained action recognition","Human motion in sports","Skeleton-based motion recognition","Temporal attention maps","Transformer model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1AE0EBB2641BB0CE1B9C0217967E75E3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102753157/Ibh_TemPose_A_New_Skeleton-Based_Transformer_Model_Designed_for_Fine-Grained_Motion_CVPRW_2023_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023W/CVSports/papers/Ibh_TemPose_A_New_Skeleton-Based_Transformer_Model_Designed_for_Fine-Grained_Motion_CVPRW_2023_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"ibhpau","last":"Ibh","locid":"91d18624-3489-48a8-834d-8737581b8ff2","name":"Ibh, Magnus","orcid":"0009-0002-0334-4151","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pascal","key":"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","name":"Madeleine, Pascal","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"2023 Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops (CVPRW)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-904a4314-ec77-4601-b2d6-5809a2b83adc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"TemPose: a new skeleton-based transformer model designed for fine-grained motion recognition in badminton","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718893","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Though continuous advances in the field of human pose estimation, it remains a challenge to retrieve high-quality recordings from real-life human motion using commodity hardware. Therefore, this work focuses on predicting and improving estimates for human motion with the aim of achieving production quality for skinned mesh animations by off-the-shelf webcams. We take advantage of recent findings in the field by employing a recurrent neural network architecture to (1) predict and (2) denoise human motion, with the intention of bridging the gap between cheap recording methods and high-quality recording. First, we propose an LSTM to predict short-term human motion, which achieves competitive results to state-of-the-art methods. Then, we adapt this model architecture and train it to clean up noisy human motion from two 3D low-quality input sources, and hence mimic a real-world scenario of recording human motion which yields noisy estimates. Experiments on simulated data show that the model is capable of significantly reducing noise, and it opens the way for future work to test the model on annotated data.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Grasshof, Stella","Bastholm, Mathias","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695298"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animation denoising","Computer vision","Reconstruction","Recurrent neural networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neural network based human motion predictor and smoother","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s42979-023-02195-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695298","identifier":[{"id":"85173924871","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d3ce6ed3-057d-474c-8d1a-7247c7ef1ed4"],"keyword":["Animation denoising","Computer vision","Recurrent neural networks","reconstruction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4000F32E69B6230BEDAB97442F15761C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s42979-023-02195-0.pdf?pdf=button","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s42979-023-02195-0","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Marionette ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"bastholmpau","last":"Bastholm","name":"Bastholm, Mathias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","marionette aps"]},"sid":["itu-d3ce6ed3-057d-474c-8d1a-7247c7ef1ed4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neural Network-Based Human Motion Predictor and Smoother","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695298","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we present an approach for combining non-rigid structure-from-motion (NRSfM) with deep generative models, and propose an efficient framework for discovering trajectories in the latent space of 2D GANs corresponding to changes in 3D geometry. Our approach uses recent advances in NRSfM and enables editing of the camera and non-rigid shape information associated with the latent codes without needing to retrain the generator. This formulation provides an implicit dense 3D reconstruction as it enables the image synthesis of novel shapes from arbitrary view angles and non-rigid structure. The method is built upon a sparse backbone, where a neural regressor is first trained to regress parameters describing the cameras and sparse non-rigid structure directly from the latent codes. The latent trajectories associated with changes in the camera and structure parameters are then identified by estimating the local inverse of the regressor in the neighborhood of a given latent code. The experiments show that our approach provides a versatile, systematic way to model, analyze, and edit the geometry and non-rigid structures of faces.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Haas, René","Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712543"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["3D Geometry Editing","Deep generative models","Latent Space Trajectories","Non rigid Structure from Motion","Sparse Neural Regressor"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"controllable gan synthesis using non rigid structure from motion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2211.07195","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712543","ids":["itu-9c146d5b-4be2-4a1c-9750-7232f5f4a1c6"],"keyword":["3D Geometry Editing","Deep Generative Models","Latent Space Trajectories","Non-rigid Structure-from-Motion","Sparse Neural Regressor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F11281333CB29EECE5397E58A1D6C8F6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023W/GCV/html/Haas_Controllable_GAN_Synthesis_Using_Non-Rigid_Structure-From-Motion_CVPRW_2023_paper.html","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2211.07195","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"haaspau","last":"Haas","name":"Haas, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-9c146d5b-4be2-4a1c-9750-7232f5f4a1c6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Controllable GAN Synthesis Using Non-Rigid Structure-From-Motion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712543","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents TemPose, a novel skeleton-based transformer model designed for fine-grained motion recognition to improve understanding of the detailed player actions in badminton. The model utilizes multiple temporal and interaction layers to capture variable-length multi-person human actions while minimizing reliance on non-human visual context. TemPose is evaluated on two fine-grained badminton datasets, where it significantly outperforms other baseline models by incorporating additional input streams, such as the shuttlecock position, into the temporal transformer layers of the model. Additionally, TemPose demonstrates great versatility by achieving competitive results compared to other state-of-the-art skeleton-based models on the large-scale action recognition benchmark NTU RGB+D. Experiments are conducted to explore how different model parameter configurations affect Tem-Pose's performance. Additionally, a qualitative analysis of the temporal attention maps suggests that the model learns to prioritize frames of specific poses relevant to different actions while formulating an intuition of each individual's importance in the sequences. Overall, TemPose is an intuitive and versatile architecture that has the potential to be further developed and incorporated into other methods for managing human motion in sports with state-of-the-art results.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ibh, Magnus","Grasshof, Stella","Witzner, Dan","Madeleine, Pascal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-726183"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-22","place":"Vancouver, ca","start":"2023-06-18","title":"2023 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops, CVPRW 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ibh, Magnus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tempose a new skeleton based transformer model designed for fine grained motion recognition in badminton","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/700594667/TemPose_CVPRSubmitted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Acknowledgements. We acknowledge the financial support from the Novo Nordisk Fonden as a part of Team-SPORTek, which enabled us to conduct this research. We would also like to thank Badminton Danmark and Team Danmark for their contributions to this study, including data collection and expert insights into badminton."],"id":"S01-000.00-726183","identifier":[{"id":"85170822333","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b6c6fb34-1540-4dd3-a894-cfdfe871eb0b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B3931B7C05373552108CF91D7A903E23"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/700594667/TemPose_CVPRSubmitted.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, ExerciseTech"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"ibhpau","last":"Ibh","name":"Ibh, Magnus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","name":"Grasshof, Stella","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"witznerpau","last":"Witzner","name":"Witzner, Dan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pascal","key":"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","locid":"2fa369c5-96e8-43bb-8c9d-1331827e6802","name":"Madeleine, Pascal","orcid":"0000-0002-2164-234X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cvprw59228.2023.00548","eisbn":["9798350302493"],"isbn":["9798350302509"],"issn":["21607508"],"pages":"5199-5208","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE Computer Society Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops","status":"p","title":"Proceedings - 2023 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops, CVPRW 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170822333"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b6c6fb34-1540-4dd3-a894-cfdfe871eb0b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"TemPose : a new skeleton-based transformer model designed for fine-grained motion recognition in badminton","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-726183","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we use a tensor model based on the Higher-Order Singular Value Decomposition (HOSVD) to discover semantic directions in Generative Adversarial Networks. This is achieved by first embedding a structured facial expression database into the latent space using the e4e encoder. Specifically, we discover directions in latent space corresponding to the six prototypical emotions: anger, disgust, fear, happiness, sadness, and surprise, as well as a direction for yaw rotation. These latent space directions are employed to change the expression or yaw rotation of real face images. We compare our found directions to similar directions found by two other methods. The results show that the visual quality of the resultant edits are on par with State-of-the-Art. It can also be concluded that the tensor-based model is well suited for emotion and yaw editing, i.e., that the emotion or yaw rotation of a novel face image can be robustly changed without a significant effect on identity or other attributes in the images.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Haas, René","Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384783"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition","Face Synthesis","Generative adversarial network"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tensor based emotion editing in the stylegan latent space","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.06102","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384783","ids":["itu-eea42dca-6570-4bfe-ae45-18a9b15afdca"],"keyword":["Computer vision and pattern recognition","Face Synthesis","generative adversarial network"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F995BED9613C9FCA062262739F0DEBA6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.06102","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"haaspau","last":"Haas","name":"Haas, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-eea42dca-6570-4bfe-ae45-18a9b15afdca"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tensor-based Emotion Editing in the StyleGAN Latent Space","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384783","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Recording real life human motion as a skinned mesh animation with an acceptable quality is usually difficult. Even though recent advances in pose estimation have enabled motion capture from off-the-shelf webcams, the low quality makes it infeasible for use in production quality animation. This work proposes to use recent advances in the prediction of human motion through neural networks to augment low quality human motion, in an effort to bridge the gap between cheap recording methods and high quality recording. First, a model, competitive with prior work in short-term human motion prediction, is constructed. Then, the model is trained to clean up motion from two low quality input sources, mimicking a real world scenario of recording human motion through two webcams. Experiments on simulated data show that the model is capable of significantly reducing noise, and it opens the way for future work to test the model on annotated data.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bastholm, Mathias","Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384236"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animation","Denoising","Motion capture","Noise","Recurrent neural networks","body motion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neural network based human motion smoother","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569437/ICPRAM2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384236","identifier":[{"id":"85173943994","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ca7722df-15e0-463f-8bcf-2ef2ae689980"],"keyword":["animation","body motion","denoising","motion capture","noise","recurrent neural networks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-262F115295E3E4409607B5CDA06F4CF7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569437/ICPRAM2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"bastholmpau","last":"Bastholm","name":"Bastholm, Mathias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"SCITEPRESS Digital Library","status":"p","title":"International Conference on Pattern Recognition Applications and Methods (ICPRA) 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ca7722df-15e0-463f-8bcf-2ef2ae689980"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neural Network-Based Human Motion Smoother","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384236","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this work we present a method that combines tensor-based face modelling and analysis and non-rigid structure-from-motion (NRSFM). The core idea is to see that the conventional tensor formulation for the face structure and expression analysis can be utilised while the structure component can be directly analysed as the non-rigid structure-from-motion problem. To the NRSFM problem part we further present a novel prior-free approach that factorises the 2D input shapes into affine projection matrices, rank-one 3D affine basis shapes, and the basis shape coefficients. The linear combination of the basis shapes thus yields the recovered 3D shapes upto an affine transformation. In contrast to most works in literature, no calibration information of the cameras or structure prior is required. Experiments on challenging face datasets show that our method, with and without the metric upgrade, is accurate and fast when compared to the state-of-the-art and is well suitable for dense reconstruction and face editing.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382525"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Non rigid Structure from Motion","tensor model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tensor based non rigid structure from motion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569442/WACV2022_TensorNRSfM.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382525","ids":["itu-53f9665d-f889-4f89-9598-964d2faf879b"],"keyword":["non-rigid structure-from-motion","tensor model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E38BB4B244B6C888C02454BCDC0E2852"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569442/WACV2022_TensorNRSfM.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"IEEE Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (WACV) 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-53f9665d-f889-4f89-9598-964d2faf879b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tensor-Based Non-Rigid Structure from Motion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382525","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we propose tGAN a tensor-based method for modeling the latent space of generative models. The objective is to identify semantic directions in latent space. To this end, we propose to fit a multilinear tensor model on a structured facial expression database, which is initially embedded into latent space. We validate our approach on StyleGAN trained on FFHQ using BU-3DFE as a structured facial expression database. We show how the parameters of the multilinear tensor model can be approximated by Alternating Least Squares. Further, we introduce a stacked style-separated tensor model, defined as an ensemble of style-specific models to integrate our approach with the extended latent space of StyleGAN. We show that taking the individual styles of the extended latent space into account leads to higher model flexibility and lower reconstruction error. Finally, we do several experiments comparing our approach to former work on both GANs and multilinear models. Concretely, we analyze the expression subspace and find that the expression trajectories meet at an apathetic face that is consistent with earlier work. We also show that by changing the pose of a person, the generated image from our approach is closer to the ground truth than results from two competing approaches.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Haas, René","Grasshof, Stella","Brandt, Sami Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383429"],"event":{"acronym":"FG (alt: FGR)","title":"IEEE International Conference on Automatic Face and Gesture Recognition"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["StyleGAN","tensor model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tensor based subspace factorization for stylegan","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569470/FG2021.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383429","ids":["itu-932f1dd9-d173-4714-a623-bbccc7b41226"],"keyword":["StyleGAN","tensor model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-69F03E70765E3C16E62F13EA038D0D5E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/356026652_Tensor-based_Subspace_Factorization_for_StyleGAN","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86569470/FG2021.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"haaspau","last":"Haas","name":"Haas, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"IEEE International Conference on Automatic Face and Gesture Recognition 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-932f1dd9-d173-4714-a623-bbccc7b41226"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tensor-based Subspace Factorization for StyleGAN","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383429","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In this work, we present a new versatile 3D multilinear statistical face model, based on a tensor factorisation of 3D face scans, that decomposes the shapes into person and expression subspaces. Investigation of the expression subspace reveals an inherent low-dimensional substructure, and further, a star-shaped structure. This is due to two novel findings. (1) Increasing the strength of one emotion approximately forms a linear trajectory in the subspace. (2) All these trajectories intersect at a single point - not at the neutral expression as assumed by almost all prior works - but at an apathetic expression. We utilise these structural findings by reparameterising the expression subspace by the fourth-order moment tensor centred at the point of apathy. We propose a 3D face reconstruction method from single or multiple 2D projections by assuming an uncalibrated projective camera model. The non-linearity caused by the perspective projection can be neatly included into the model. The proposed algorithm separates person and expression subspaces convincingly, and enables flexible, natural modelling of expressions for a wide variety of human faces. Applying the method on independent faces showed that morphing between different persons and expressions can be performed without strong deformations.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Grasshof, Stella","Ackermann, Hanno","Brandt, Sami Sebastian","Ostermann, Jorn"],"cuid":["S02-094.59-038333"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz University Hannover","Leibniz Universität Hannover","University of Hanover"],"keyword":["3D reconstruction","HOSVD","Statistical shape model","expression transfer","person transfer","tensor model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multilinear modelling of faces and expressions","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86353553/tpami_pure.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-094.59-038333","identifier":[{"id":"85114612751","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32305893","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["itu-7aabbc12-7aeb-4bc2-8472-de92e1b3d9cd","ku-049650b6-2e5d-4624-a656-b92e6360f964"],"keyword":["3D-reconstruction","HOSVD","Statistical shape model","expression transfer","person transfer","tensor model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AA5FC79F751578EE6CD0CF951C3F7A4A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86353553/tpami_pure.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"leibniz universität hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Universität Hannover","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of hanover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Hanover","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"leibniz university hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz University Hannover","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanno","key":"ackermannpau","last":"Ackermann","name":"Ackermann, Hanno","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 1","first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"16b4d290-9775-4705-8e06-382641f16444","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jörn","key":"ostermannpau","last":"Ostermann","name":"Ostermann, Jörn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32305893"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tpami.2020.2986496","issn":["01628828"],"issue":"10","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence","pages":"3540-3554","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114612751"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7aabbc12-7aeb-4bc2-8472-de92e1b3d9cd","ku-049650b6-2e5d-4624-a656-b92e6360f964"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multilinear Modelling of Faces and Expressions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.59-038333","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We propose a general, prior-free approach for the uncalibrated non-rigid structure-from-motion problem for modelling and analysis of non-rigid objects such as human faces. We recover the non-rigid affine structure and motion from 2D point correspondences by assuming that (1) the non-rigid shapes are generated by a linear combination of rigid 3D basis shapes, (2) that the non-rigid shapes are affine in nature, i.e., they can be modelled as deviations from the mean, rigid shape, (3) and that the basis shapes are statistically independent. In contrast to the majority of existing works, no statistical prior is assumed for the structure and motion apart from the assumption the that underlying basis shapes are statistically independent. The independent 3D shape bases are recovered by independent subspace analysis (ISA). Likewise, in contrast to the most previous approaches, no calibration information is assumed for affine cameras; the reconstruction is solved up to a global affine ambiguity that makes our approach simple and efficient. In the experiments, we evaluated the method with several standard data sets including a real face expression data set of 7200 faces with 2D point correspondences and unknown 3D structure and motion for which we obtained promising results.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Brandt, Sami Sebastian","Ackermann, Hanno","Grasshof, Stella"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381372"],"event":{"acronym":"ICCV","title":"International Conference on Computer Vision"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz Universität Hannover"],"keyword":["3D Shape Reconstruction","Affine Structure Recovery","Independent Subspace Analysis","Statistical Independence","Uncalibrated Non Rigid Structure from Motion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uncalibrated non rigid factorisation by independent subspace analysis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85683429/Brandt_Uncalibrated_Non_Rigid_Factorisation_by_Independent_Subspace_Analysis_ICCVW_2019_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381372","identifier":[{"id":"85082448778","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-076bc7b5-64f8-475c-8b8e-97efd82c09e1"],"keyword":["3D Shape Reconstruction","Affine Structure Recovery","Independent Subspace Analysis","Statistical Independence","Uncalibrated Non-Rigid Structure-from-Motion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-54CA640F0EB9AF76A7D0D2B6C0065D80"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85683429/Brandt_Uncalibrated_Non_Rigid_Factorisation_by_Independent_Subspace_Analysis_ICCVW_2019_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://openaccess.thecvf.com/content_ICCVW_2019/papers/RSL-CV/Brandt_Uncalibrated_Non-Rigid_Factorisation_by_Independent_Subspace_Analysis_ICCVW_2019_paper.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"leibniz universität hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Universität Hannover","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanno","key":"ackermannpau","last":"Ackermann","name":"Ackermann, Hanno","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","name":"Grasshof, Stella","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iccvw.2019.00070","eisbn":["9781728150239"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2019 IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision Workshop (ICCVW)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082448778"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-076bc7b5-64f8-475c-8b8e-97efd82c09e1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Uncalibrated Non-Rigid Factorisation by Independent Subspace Analysis","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381372","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We propose a general, prior-free approach for the uncalibrated non-rigid structure-from-motion problem for modelling and analysis of non-rigid objects such as human faces. The word general refers to an approach that recovers the non-rigid affine structure and motion from 2D point correspondences by assuming that (1) the non-rigid shapes are generated by a linear combination of rigid 3D basis shapes, (2) that the non-rigid shapes are affine in nature, i.e., they can be modelled as deviations from the mean, rigid shape, (3) and that the basis shapes are statistically independent. In contrast to the majority of existing works, no prior information is assumed for the structure and motion apart from the assumption the that underlying basis shapes are statistically independent. The independent 3D shape bases are recovered by independent subspace analysis (ISA). Likewise, in contrast to the most previous approaches, no calibration information is assumed for affine cameras; the reconstruction is solved up to a global affine ambiguity that makes our approach simple but efficient. In the experiments, we evaluated the method with several standard data sets including a real face expression data set of 7200 faces with 2D point correspondences and unknown 3D structure and motion for which we obtained promising results.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Brandt, Sami Sebastian","Ackermann, Hanno","Grasshof, Stella"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384987"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz Universität Hannover"],"keyword":["Computer vision","Non rigid Structure from Motion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uncalibrated non rigid factorisation by independent subspace analysis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83658175/1811.09132v1.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384987","ids":["itu-fd26f88b-1c21-4e89-b8bf-b1f01c28dbe5"],"keyword":["computer vision","non-rigid structure-from-motion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1D5737FBE3CF3333135CD2B9F49D7C8F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83658175/1811.09132v1.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"leibniz universität hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Universität Hannover","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sami Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"e8e88610-5144-41da-95bf-597abf1d7869","name":"Brandt, Sami Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-2141-9815","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanno","key":"ackermannpau","last":"Ackermann","name":"Ackermann, Hanno","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","name":"Grasshof, Stella","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fd26f88b-1c21-4e89-b8bf-b1f01c28dbe5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Uncalibrated Non-Rigid Factorisation by Independent Subspace Analysis","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384987","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
